/-!
# The spectral sequence for a smooth morphism

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of schemes over a base `S`, with `g : Y ⟶ S` the structure
morphism of the target. Smoothness of `f` makes the sequence of relative differentials

`0 ⟶ f^*Ω_{Y/S} ⟶ Ω_{X/S} ⟶ Ω_{X/Y} ⟶ 0`

locally split, and the resulting two-step filtration of `Ω_{X/S}` induces on `Ω^•_{X/S}` the
decreasing filtration whose `k`-th step `F^kΩ^•_{X/S}` is generated by the forms pulled back
from `Y`; by the Leibniz rule each step is a subcomplex, the filtration is exhaustive
(`F^k = Ω^•_{X/S}` for `k ≤ 0`), and `F^kΩ^p_{X/S} = 0` for `p < k`, with graded pieces

`gr^kΩ^•_{X/S} = f^{-1}Ω^k_{Y/S}[-k] ⊗_{f^{-1}𝒪_Y} Ω^•_{X/Y}`.

Feeding this filtered complex to the spectral sequence of a filtered complex
([Stacks, Tag 0FLL]) and identifying `Rf_*gr^kΩ^•_{X/S} = Ω^k_{Y/S}[-k] ⊗^{\mathbf L}_{𝒪_Y}
Rf_*Ω^•_{X/Y}` by [Stacks, Tag 0FML] gives a bounded spectral sequence with first page

`E_1^{p, q} = H^q(Ω^p_{Y/S} ⊗^{\mathbf L}_{𝒪_Y} Rf_*Ω^•_{X/Y})`

abutting to `R^{p + q}f_*Ω^•_{X/S}`. That is the content of [Stacks, Tag 0FMM], proved here from
the filtration and the identification of its graded pieces.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.inverseImageMap`: for a ringed space `(X, 𝒪_X)` and continuous
  maps `i : Z ⟶ W` and `j : W ⟶ X`, the canonical morphism of ringed spaces
  `(Z, (i ∘ j)^{-1}𝒪_X) ⟶ (W, j^{-1}𝒪_X)` over `i`.
* `Stacks.DeRhamSmooth.relativeBase`: the morphism of ringed spaces
  `(X, (f ∘ g)^{-1}𝒪_S) ⟶ (Y, g^{-1}𝒪_S)` along which `Ω^•_{X/S}` is pushed forward.
* `Stacks.DeRhamSmooth.derivedRelativePushforward` and
  `Stacks.DeRhamSmooth.derivedRelativePushforwardUnit`: the unbounded derived pushforward
  `Rf_*` of `(f ∘ g)^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules along `relativeBase`, with its derived-functor unit.
* `Stacks.DeRhamSmooth.deRhamHigherDirectImage`: **`R^nf_*Ω^•_{X/S}`**, a sheaf of
  `g^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules on `Y`.
* `Stacks.DeRhamSmooth.deRhamFirstPage`: **`H^q(Ω^p_{Y/S} ⊗^{\mathbf L}_{𝒪_Y}
  Rf_*Ω^•_{X/Y})`**, read as a sheaf of `g^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules by restriction of scalars.

## Main results

* `Stacks.DeRhamSmooth.exists_boundedDeRhamSpectralSequence`: **[Stacks, Tag 0FMM]**, the
  bounded spectral sequence with first page `deRhamFirstPage` abutting to
  `deRhamHigherDirectImage`.

## Implementation notes

The de Rham differential is only `(f ∘ g)^{-1}𝒪_S`-linear, so `Ω^•_{X/S}` is a complex of
`(f ∘ g)^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules and its direct image is taken along `relativeBase`, landing in
`g^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules; the spectral sequence therefore lives in `Mod(g^{-1}𝒪_S)` and its first
page is the restriction of scalars along `g^{-1}𝒪_S ⟶ 𝒪_Y` of an `𝒪_Y`-module. Restriction of
scalars along that map is `Stacks.DeRhamDirectImage.toInverseImageBase`-pushforward, by
`Stacks.DeRhamDirectImage.pushforward_toInverseImageBase`, so no second spelling of it is
introduced.

`relativeBase` is a genuine construction, not a choice: a morphism of ringed spaces with
underlying map `f` into `(Y, g^{-1}𝒪_S)` amounts, by the inverse-image/direct-image adjunction
for `g`, to a map `𝒪_S ⟶ (f ∘ g)_*(f ∘ g)^{-1}𝒪_S`, and `inverseImageMap` takes it to be the
unit. This uses that the direct image along a composite of continuous maps is the composite of
the direct images, which holds on the nose for sheaves on topological spaces.

The derived pushforward used is the total right derived functor of the pushforward on the
homotopy category, so `deRhamHigherDirectImage` names one definite sheaf rather than one
depending on a chosen derived functor; the spectral sequence is produced by
`Stacks.Cohomology.FilteredComplex.relativeSpectralSequence_of_filteredKInjectiveResolution` at
that functor, with the filtered K-injective resolution of [Stacks, Tag 0BKI].

The filtration itself is a hypothesis. What is granted is the filtered complex
`F^•Ω^•_{X/S}` of Section 0FMK (`K`, `hKX`), its exhaustion (`hexh`, from which the
`p ≪ 0` clause of Tag 0FLL is derived here), the vanishing of `R^nf_*F^pΩ^•_{X/S}` for
`p ≫ 0` (`hvanish`, which is the boundedness coming from `F^pΩ^q_{X/S} = 0` for `q < p`),
and the identification of `R^{p + q}f_*gr^pΩ^•_{X/S}` with
`H^q(Ω^p_{Y/S} ⊗^{\mathbf L}_{𝒪_Y} Rf_*Ω^•_{X/Y})` (`hgr`), which is the computation of the
graded pieces in Section 0FMK followed by the projection formula of [Stacks, Tag 0FML].

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FMM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FMM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FMK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FMK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FML](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FML)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FLL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FLL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BKI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BKI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BDU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BDU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction Stacks.Cohomology.FilteredComplex Stacks.DeRhamDirectImage

attribute [local instance 2000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace

/-- The canonical morphism of ringed spaces `(Z, (i ∘ j)^{-1}𝒪_X) ⟶ (W, j^{-1}𝒪_X)` attached to
continuous maps `i : Z ⟶ W` and `j : W ⟶ X` and a ringed space `(X, 𝒪_X)`: its underlying
continuous map is `i`, and its structure map `j^{-1}𝒪_X ⟶ i_*(i ∘ j)^{-1}𝒪_X` is the adjoint
of the unit `𝒪_X ⟶ (i ∘ j)_*(i ∘ j)^{-1}𝒪_X` under the inverse-image/direct-image adjunction
for `j`, the direct image along `i ∘ j` being the direct image along `j` of the direct image
along `i`. -/
def inverseImageMap (X : RingedSpace.{u, u}) {Z W : TopCat.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ W)
    (j : W ⟶ X.carrier) : inverseImage X (i ≫ j) ⟶ inverseImage X j :=
  InducedCategory.homMk
    { base := i
      c := (((TopCat.Sheaf.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction CommRingCat.{u} j).homEquiv X.sheaf
              ((TopCat.Sheaf.pushforward CommRingCat.{u} i).obj
                ((TopCat.Sheaf.pullback CommRingCat.{u} (i ≫ j)).obj X.sheaf))).symm
            ((TopCat.Sheaf.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction CommRingCat.{u} (i ≫ j)).unit.app
              X.sheaf)).hom }

/-- The underlying continuous map of `inverseImageMap X i j` is `i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem inverseImageMap_base (X : RingedSpace.{u, u}) {Z W : TopCat.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ W)
    (j : W ⟶ X.carrier) : (inverseImageMap X i j).hom.base = i :=
  rfl

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace

namespace Stacks.DeRhamSmooth

variable {X Y S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Y ⟶ S)

/-- The morphism of ringed spaces `(X, (f ∘ g)^{-1}𝒪_S) ⟶ (Y, g^{-1}𝒪_S)` with underlying map
that of `f`. The relative de Rham complex `Ω^•_{X/S}` is a complex of
`(f ∘ g)^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules, so this is the morphism along which it is pushed forward to `Y`. -/
abbrev relativeBase : inverseImageBase (f ≫ g) ⟶ inverseImageBase g :=
  RingedSpace.inverseImageMap S.toRingedSpace f.base g.base

/-- The unbounded derived pushforward `Rf_* : D((f ∘ g)^{-1}𝒪_S) ⥤ D(g^{-1}𝒪_S)`, taken as the
total right derived functor of the pushforward along `relativeBase` on the homotopy category of
cochain complexes. -/
abbrev derivedRelativePushforward :
    DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (inverseImageBase (f ≫ g)))) ⥤
      DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (inverseImageBase g))) :=
  (homotopyPushforward (relativeBase f g)).totalRightDerived DerivedCategory.Qh
    (HomotopyCategory.quasiIso
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (inverseImageBase (f ≫ g)))) (ComplexShape.up ℤ))

/-- The derived-functor unit of `derivedRelativePushforward`. -/
abbrev derivedRelativePushforwardUnit :
    homotopyPushforward (relativeBase f g) ⟶
      DerivedCategory.Qh ⋙ derivedRelativePushforward f g :=
  (homotopyPushforward (relativeBase f g)).totalRightDerivedUnit DerivedCategory.Qh
    (HomotopyCategory.quasiIso
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (inverseImageBase (f ≫ g)))) (ComplexShape.up ℤ))

/-- **`R^nf_*Ω^•_{X/S}`**, the `n`-th higher direct image along `f` of the relative de Rham
complex of `X` over the base `S`: a sheaf of `g^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules on `Y`. -/
def deRhamHigherDirectImage (n : ℤ) : Modules (inverseImageBase g) :=
  higherDirectImage (derivedRelativePushforward f g) (deRhamCochainComplex (f ≫ g)) n

/-- **`H^q(Ω^p_{Y/S} ⊗^{\mathbf L}_{𝒪_Y} Rf_*Ω^•_{X/Y})`**, the first page of the spectral
sequence of a smooth morphism: the `q`-th cohomology sheaf of the derived tensor product over
`𝒪_Y` of the sheaf `Ω^p_{Y/S}` of relative `p`-forms of `Y` over `S` with the derived direct
image of the relative de Rham complex of `X` over `Y`, read as a sheaf of `g^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules
by restriction of scalars along `g^{-1}𝒪_S ⟶ 𝒪_Y`. -/
def deRhamFirstPage (p q : ℤ) : Modules (inverseImageBase g) :=
  (pushforward (toInverseImageBase g)).obj
    ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (StrictlyPerfect.OXMod.{u, u, u} Y.toRingedSpace) q).obj
      (((Stacks.Cohomology.TorAmplitude.derTensor Y.toRingedSpace).tensor.obj
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (StrictlyPerfect.OXMod.{u, u, u} Y.toRingedSpace) 0).obj
          (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms g p))).obj
        (DerivedCategory.Plus.ι.obj (derivedDeRhamDirectImage f))))

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0FMM.** Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a quasi-compact, quasi-separated and smooth
morphism of schemes over a base `S`, with `g : Y ⟶ S` the structure morphism of the target.
There is a bounded cohomological spectral sequence of sheaves of `g^{-1}𝒪_S`-modules on `Y`,
starting at its first page, with

`E_1^{p, q} = H^q(Ω^p_{Y/S} ⊗^{\mathbf L}_{𝒪_Y} Rf_*Ω^•_{X/Y})`,

which abuts to `R^{p + q}f_*Ω^•_{X/S}`.

The filtration of `Ω^•_{X/S}` by the forms pulled back from `Y` is supplied as the filtered
complex `K` with `K.X = Ω^•_{X/S}`, together with its exhaustion `hexh`, the eventual vanishing
`hvanish` of the higher direct images of its far steps, and the identification `hgr` of
`R^{p + q}f_*gr^pK` with the first page; `hgr` is the computation of the graded pieces
`gr^kΩ^•_{X/S} = f^{-1}Ω^k_{Y/S}[-k] ⊗_{f^{-1}𝒪_Y} Ω^•_{X/Y}` of Section 0FMK followed by the
projection formula of Tag 0FML. The spectral sequence, its boundedness in the sense of Tag
0BDU, and its abutment are then those of the filtered complex `K`. -/
@[stacks 0FMM "granted the filtration of Section 0FMK as the hypotheses K, hKX, hexh and \
hvanish, and its graded pieces together with Tag 0FML as the hypothesis hgr"]
theorem exists_boundedDeRhamSpectralSequence
    [QuasiCompact f] [QuasiSeparated f] [Smooth f]
    (K : CochainComplex.Filtered (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (inverseImageBase (f ≫ g)))))
    (hKX : K.X = deRhamCochainComplex (f ≫ g))
    (hexh : ∀ p : ℤ, p ≤ 0 → IsIso (K.filtration.ι.app (op p)))
    (hvanish : ∀ n : ℤ, ∃ p₀ : ℤ, ∀ p : ℤ, p₀ ≤ p →
      IsZero (higherDirectImage (derivedRelativePushforward f g)
        (K.filtration.obj (op p)) n))
    (hgr : ∀ p q : ℤ, Nonempty (higherDirectImage (derivedRelativePushforward f g)
      ((FilteredObject.gr p).obj K) (p + q) ≅ deRhamFirstPage f g p q)) :
    ∃ E : CohomologicalSpectralSequence
        (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (inverseImageBase g))) 1,
      _root_.IsBounded E ∧
      (∀ p q : ℤ, Nonempty ((E.page 1).X (p, q) ≅ deRhamFirstPage f g p q)) ∧
      SpectralSequence.AbutsTo E (fun n => deRhamHigherDirectImage f g n) := by
  have hexhaust : ∀ n : ℤ, ∃ p₁ : ℤ, ∀ p : ℤ, p ≤ p₁ →
      IsIso (higherDirectImageMap (derivedRelativePushforward f g)
        (K.filtration.ι.app (op p)) n) := by
    refine fun n => ⟨0, fun p hp => ?_⟩
    have := hexh p hp
    unfold higherDirectImageMap
    infer_instance
  have hpt := hasPointwiseRightDerivedFunctor_homotopyPushforward (relativeBase f g)
  have hRf : (derivedRelativePushforward f g).IsRightDerivedFunctor
      (derivedRelativePushforwardUnit f g)
      (HomotopyCategory.quasiIso
        (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (inverseImageBase (f ≫ g)))) (ComplexShape.up ℤ)) :=
    inferInstance
  obtain ⟨J, j, h⟩ := Stacks.Injectives.exists_filtered_quasiIso_isKInjective K
  -- The twelve conclusions of [Stacks, Tag 0BKI] are read off by projection rather than
  -- destructured, each `obtain` building a motive over the conclusions below it.
  have hIStep := h.2.1
  have hKI := h.2.2.2.2.1
  have hKIStep := h.2.2.2.2.2.1
  have hKISubquot := h.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.1
  have hj := h.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.1
  have hjStep := h.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.1
  have hjSubquot := h.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2
  have hKIGraded (p : ℤ) : ((FilteredObject.gr p).obj J).IsKInjective :=
    hKISubquot p (p + 1) (by omega)
  have hjGraded (p : ℤ) : QuasiIso ((FilteredObject.gr p).map j) :=
    hjSubquot p (p + 1) (by omega)
  obtain ⟨hpage, hconv⟩ := relativeSpectralSequence_of_filteredKInjectiveResolution
    (relativeBase f g) (derivedRelativePushforward f g) (derivedRelativePushforwardUnit f g)
    K J hRf j hj hjStep hjGraded hIStep hKI hKIStep hKIGraded
  obtain ⟨hfin, F, hF, hFeq, hbounds, hinf, hgriso⟩ := hconv hvanish hexhaust
  have hH : (fun n : ℤ => higherDirectImage (derivedRelativePushforward f g) K.X n) =
      fun n : ℤ => deRhamHigherDirectImage f g n := by
    simp only [deRhamHigherDirectImage, hKX]
  refine ⟨(pushforwardSpectralSequence (relativeBase f g) J).shiftStart (by omega), hfin,
    fun p q => ⟨(hpage p q).some ≪≫ (hgr p q).some⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [← hH]
  exact SpectralSequence.AbutsTo.shiftStart ⟨hinf, F, hF, hbounds, hgriso⟩ (by omega)

end Stacks.DeRhamSmooth

end
